# Exploration Report: Owners / sharesHousehold / householdId

## Key finding up front
`sharesHousehold` is **already fully implemented** (as a request-only, write-only flag that suppresses the duplicate-household rejection). `householdId` **does NOT exist anywhere** in the code — not on the entity, not in the OpenAPI schema, not in any function, and is not stored or returned. The one existing test (`coreJoinersShareHouseholdId`) expects a persisted, returned `householdId` that is shared across co-household owners, so that is the gap to implement.

Build system: **Maven** (wrapper `./mvnw`; `pom.xml`). No Gradle. DTOs are **generated** by the `openapi-generator-maven-plugin` from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` into `target/generated-sources/openapi/...` (package `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`). There is no hand-written `OwnerRequest`/`OwnerResponse`; the request DTO is the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` and the response DTO is the generated `OwnerDto`.

Run the owner tests:
```
./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest
```
(There is a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, extending `AcceptanceBase`. To run just the one method: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest#coreJoinersShareHouseholdId`.)

---

## 1. Owner-related code structure

Entity / repo / mapper (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/`):
- `model/Owner.java` — JPA entity. Fields: address, city, telephone, email, registrationDate, customerCode, pets. **No householdId / sharesHousehold.**
- `repository/OwnerRepository.java` — interface (findByLastName, findById, save, findAll, delete; plus paged variants).
- `repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java` — implementations.
- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — MapStruct mapping Owner ↔ OwnerDto/OwnerFieldsDto/OwnerPageDto.

DTOs (generated from `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, schemas `OwnerFields`, `Owner`, `OwnerPage` → `OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`, `OwnerPageDto`). `OwnerFieldsDto` already carries `sharesHousehold` (writeOnly); `OwnerDto` extends it adding id, displayName, initials, customerCode, pets. **No householdId in either schema.**

OfficeFloor function classes (`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/`): `ValidateOwner`, `CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique`, `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`, `BuildOwner`, `AssignCustomerCode`, `SaveOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `LoadOwner`, `ApplyOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`, `RespondWithOwner`, `DeleteOwner`, `ListOwners`, `ListOwnersPage`, `BuildOwnersPet`, `LoadOwnersPet`, `OwnerTelephone`.

Escalations (`.../rest/escalation/`): `OwnerHouseholdDuplicateException`(+Handler), `OwnerTelephoneDuplicateException`(+Handler), `OwnerTelephoneInvalidException`(+Handler), `OwnerEmailInvalidException`(+Handler), `OwnerFieldsMissingException`(+Handler).

---

## 2. Address / lastName uniqueness / "same address already used" logic

This lives in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java`. It rejects a create with HTTP 409 (`OwnerHouseholdDuplicateException`) when another owner has the same **lastName AND address** (both normalized: stripped, internal whitespace collapsed, lower-cased), **unless** `sharesHousehold == true`, in which case the check is skipped. Full source:

```java
public class CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique {
    public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
            throws OwnerHouseholdDuplicateException {
        if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
            return; // opted in to sharing a household; skip the duplicate check
        }
        String lastName = normalize(request.getLastName());
        String address = normalize(request.getAddress());
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
                    && address.equals(normalize(existing.getAddress()))) {
                throw new OwnerHouseholdDuplicateException(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress());
            }
        }
    }
    private static String normalize(String value) {
        if (value == null) return "";
        return value.strip().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
    }
}
```

There is also a telephone-uniqueness check (`CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique`, 409 on duplicate E.164 phone). The handler `OwnerHouseholdDuplicateExceptionHandler` responds 409 with body `{"errors": ["lastName","address"]}`.

Note: `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique` runs only in the POST pipeline, not PUT.

---

## 3. Tests referencing owners / household / sharesHousehold

There is exactly **one** test file matching: `src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (plus the base `AcceptanceBase.java` and `AuditLogCapture.java`). Full `AcceptanceTest.java`:

```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.acceptance;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertTrue;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;
import tools.jackson.databind.node.ObjectNode;

/** shares-household: The request may set boolean 'sharesHousehold'. When true, allow an owner at an address alr... */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreJoinersShareHouseholdId() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode a = ownerNode();
		createOwnerOk(a);
		ObjectNode b = ownerNode(); b.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText());
		b.put("address", a.get("address").asText()); b.put("sharesHousehold", true);
		int idb = createOwnerOk(b);
		ObjectNode c = ownerNode(); c.put("lastName", a.get("lastName").asText());
		c.put("address", a.get("address").asText()); c.put("sharesHousehold", true);
		int idc = createOwnerOk(c);
		String hb = fetchOwner(idb).get("householdId").asText();
		assertEquals(hb, fetchOwner(idc).get("householdId").asText());
		assertTrue(!hb.isBlank());
	}
}
```

What this requires that does not yet exist:
- Co-household owners (same lastName + address, created with `sharesHousehold:true`) must be assigned a **persisted `householdId`** that is returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}` and is **identical** for b and c (and non-blank).
- So owner `a` (first at the address, no sharesHousehold) establishes a household; `b` and `c` joining with `sharesHousehold:true` must get the same householdId as the existing household at that name+address.

`AcceptanceBase.java` relevant helpers: `ownerNode()` builds a fully-unique valid owner (firstName "Test", unique lastName/address/city/telephone). `createOwnerOk(body)` POSTs to `/api/owners`, asserts 2xx, returns the created id (from body `id` or `Location` header). `fetchOwner(id)` GETs `/api/owners/{id}`, asserts 2xx, returns parsed JSON. Tests run `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional` (rolled back) as `@WithMockUser` admin with roles OWNER_ADMIN/VET_ADMIN/ADMIN. `AuditLogCapture.java` is a test-support bean (not household-related).

