    public void service(@Val Owner owner, @Val OwnerFieldsDto request) {
        owner.setAddress(request.getAddress());
        owner.setCity(request.getCity());
        owner.setFirstName(request.getFirstName());
        owner.setLastName(request.getLastName());
        owner.setTelephone(request.getTelephone());
        owner.setEmail(request.getEmail());
    }
}
```

`RespondWithOwnerUpdated.java`: responds `204 NO_CONTENT` with the mapped `OwnerDto` body.

---

## 6. OpenAPI schema (where householdId would be added)

`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`: `OwnerFields` (line ~1991) currently defines firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone, email, registrationDate, and `sharesHousehold` (boolean, `writeOnly: true`, "Request-only flag... Not stored or returned"). `Owner` (line ~2059) is `allOf [OwnerFields] + {id, displayName, initials, customerCode, pets}`. There is **no householdId property** in either; adding a stored, returned `householdId` (and a corresponding `Owner.householdId` entity column + assignment logic in the POST pipeline, e.g. around `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`/`BuildOwner`) is what the test requires.

Current `sharesHousehold` schema block:
```yaml
sharesHousehold:
  title: Shares household
  description: Request-only flag. When true, allows creating this owner even though another owner has the same lastName and address (i.e. they share a household). Not stored or returned.
  type: boolean
  writeOnly: true
  example: true
```

